@@ -100,19 +100,27 @@ Each pet is recorded against exactly one owner, with a name, a birth date, and a
 
 ### Visits
 
-<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a>
+<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a><a id="req-visitedit-001"></a>
 
 A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`.
 
+A booked visit can be corrected: its date and its description can be changed, so a booking recorded in error is set right without booking a second visit `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]`. Correction is offered through the visit form opened for an existing visit, with that visit's current date and description already filled in. A correction is held to the same rules as a booking — a description is required and the date must be later than today — and applying a correction updates the visit in place, leaving the pet with no additional visit. On success the corrected record is confirmed on the owner's record; on a rejected correction the form is shown again. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope (NG-5).
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given an existing booked visit, when its correction form is opened, then the form shows that visit's current date and description.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given an existing booked visit, when a changed description and a date later than today are submitted, then that visit is updated in place and the change is confirmed on the owner's record.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a valid correction to a visit, when it is applied, then the pet gains no additional visit — the same visit is updated.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a correction with a blank description, when it is submitted, then the correction is refused, the description is named, and the form is shown again.
+- `[REQ-VISITEDIT-001]` given a correction with a date of today or earlier, when it is submitted, then the correction is refused, the date is named, and the form is shown again.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. Correcting a visit reuses the booking form. As of `REQ-VISITEDIT-001` no link to the correction form appears on the owner's record — it is reachable only by staff who already know where to navigate. Whether a visible entry point is added is deferred (see Open Questions).
 
 ### Veterinarian directory
 
